From 7411fcf1e4c12b080a900bde29458f5edca72dea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pulpoff <pashkovsky@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 20:44:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] exynos-mobile: Samsung Galaxy S20 FE (r8s, Exynos 990)

U-Boot in BOOT, chainloaded by S-Boot with a FIT (Image.gz + dtb) as the
boot image's ramdisk; bootm ${prevbl_initrd_start_addr} boots it.

- pinctrl-exynos990: bank tables of the seven Exynos 990 pin controllers
  (from Linux), so gpio-keys work for the menu.
- board: r8s entry (G780F), DRAM banks from U-Boot's own devicetree only
  (S-Boot's FDT splits the high bank into 512 MiB nodes and lists the
  hypervisor's el2_earlymem as memory), DECON0 HW_SW_TRIG_CONTROL so the
  framebuffer refreshes.
- dss-ring: console appended to the debug-snapshot kernel log ring right
  after S-Boot's own log; a downstream recovery shows it in
  /proc/last_kmsg after any reset.
- exynos990-r8s.env: menu on Volume Down (mainline, Lineage Recovery,
  download mode, restart, power off) via PMU INFORM3/INFORM2; Linux is
  booted with INFORM3 = recovery so a panic lands in recovery.
  stdin/stdout are lists: a bare stdin=button-kbd makes
  input_stdio_register() assign the console before jumptable_init() and
  dereference gd->jt = NULL. No single quotes in commands (old hush).
- exynos-mobile.c: build without the fastboot configs.
